<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 08/13/97    08/06/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 24,341,000  23,549,000    22,373,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  63,718	36,558	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,804,000  35,804,000    33,990,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,996,842  35,996,842	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   08/13/97    08/06/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,687,000   3,904,000     3,927,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,498,000   4,237,000     3,729,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  2,893,000   3,304,000     3,243,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,953,000   2,113,000     2,404,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,429,000   3,220,000     3,195,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,847,000   5,012,000     3,952,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,033,000   1,759,000     1,923,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	24,341,000  23,549,000    22,373,000</p>
